  "body_html": "<h2>Problem</h2>\n<p>DrivenData's DaT Parkinson's Challenge asked for one number per 3D DaT-SPECT brain scan: the probability that the scan is abnormal. Entries were scored by log loss. It measures how far the predicted probabilities were from the truth; lower is better. So the model had to be right about how sure it was, not only about which scans look abnormal.</p>\n<p>The data was 1,362 scans from ten French hospitals, labelled by 11 nuclear medicine specialists. Scans came in 21 acquisition families with different sizes and resolutions. In the widest, the head filled about 1% of the image<sup class=\"cite\"><a href=\"#sources\" title=\"Source: vault note drivendata-dat-parkinsons-challenge\">[src]</a></sup>.</p>\n<h2>Approach</h2>\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-title\">Model architecture: two views of each scan, stacked into one calibrated probability</div><div class=\"flow\"><div class=\"stage\" style=\"flex-grow:1\"><div class=\"stage-label\">1 · Data</div><div class=\"stage-boxes\"><div class=\"box\"><div class=\"box-label\">DaT-SPECT brain scans</div><div class=\"box-detail\">Labelled normal or abnormal</div><ul class=\"box-specs\"><li>n = 1,362 (747 abnormal, 615 normal)</li><li>10 French hospitals</li><li>21 acquisition families</li><li>FOV 176–630 mm per axis</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"stage-out\">→ 3D volume, varying shape and spacing</div></div><div class=\"arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div><div class=\"stage\" style=\"flex-grow:1\"><div class=\"stage-label\">2 · Preprocess</div><div class=\"stage-boxes\"><div class=\"box\"><div class=\"box-label\">Standardise</div><div class=\"box-detail\">Same geometry and intensity scale for every scan</div><ul class=\"box-specs\"><li>Reorient to RAS</li><li>Resample to 2.0 mm isotropic</li><li>Centre-of-mass crop 96 × 96 × 96</li><li>Reference-region intensity normalisation</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"stage-out\">→ 1 × 96³ tensor</div></div><div class=\"arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div><div class=\"stage stage--parallel\" style=\"flex-grow:1.9\"><div class=\"stage-label\">3 · Two models in parallel</div><div class=\"stage-boxes\"><div class=\"box\"><div class=\"box-label\">3D ResNet ensemble</div><div class=\"box-detail\">10 CNNs: 2 training runs × 5 stratified folds</div><ul class=\"box-specs\"><li>GroupNorm, widths 16/32/64/128, dropout 0.3</li><li>AdamW lr 3e-4, cosine, 30 epochs, early stopping</li><li>Run 2 augmentation: elastic, PSF blur, signed gamma, count noise, mixup</li><li>No left–right flip: asymmetry is signal</li><li>TTA: 9 laterality-preserving views, logit mean</li></ul><div class=\"box-metrics\"><span class=\"chip\"><b>AUROC</b> 0.9393</span><span class=\"chip\"><b>ECE</b> 0.0187</span><span class=\"chip\"><b>log loss</b> 0.3021</span></div></div><div class=\"box\"><div class=\"box-label\">Striatal features → LightGBM</div><div class=\"box-detail\">157 hand-built SBR-style striatal features</div><ul class=\"box-specs\"><li>Logit correlation with the CNN ensemble ρ = 0.821</li></ul><div class=\"box-metrics\"><span class=\"chip\"><b>AUROC</b> 0.9184</span><span class=\"chip\"><b>ECE</b> 0.0329</span><span class=\"chip\"><b>log loss</b> 0.3659</span></div></div></div><div class=\"stage-out\">→ 2 logits per scan</div></div><div class=\"arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div><div class=\"stage\" style=\"flex-grow:1\"><div class=\"stage-label\">4 · Combine</div><div class=\"stage-boxes\"><div class=\"box\"><div class=\"box-label\">Logistic stack</div><div class=\"box-detail\">3 parameters, scored by cross-validation</div><ul class=\"box-specs\"><li>CNN +0.694, trees +0.364, intercept +0.048</li><li>Carries the calibration: no separate temperature</li><li>Clip to [1e-6, 1 − 1e-6]</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"stage-out\">→ p(abnormal)</div></div><div class=\"arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div><div class=\"stage stage--out\" style=\"flex-grow:1\"><div class=\"stage-label\">5 · Output</div><div class=\"stage-boxes\"><div class=\"box\"><div class=\"box-label\">Probability the scan is abnormal</div><div class=\"box-detail\">Final model (candidate B), out of fold</div><div class=\"box-metrics\"><span class=\"chip\"><b>AUROC</b> 0.9455</span></div></div></div></div></div><figcaption>All metrics are 5-fold stratified out-of-fold (OOF) on n = 1,362. AUROC: how well the model ranks abnormal above normal scans (1 = perfect). ECE: expected calibration error, the average gap between predicted probability and observed rate (0 = perfect).</figcaption></figure>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Crop around the brain, not the image.</strong> A fixed centre crop cut off the striatum, the region that matters, in wide scans. Each scan is cropped around its centre of mass instead.</li>\n<li><strong>Never flip left and right.</strong> Abnormality is often one-sided, and mirroring a scan would blur that signal.</li>\n<li><strong>Two different model families.</strong> The tree model on hand-built striatal measurements is weaker alone. But its outputs correlate only 0.821 with the CNN's, so it is wrong on different scans. It carries 34% of the weight in the final stack, and adding it cut log loss by 0.0184 at 3.3 sigma<sup class=\"cite\"><a href=\"#sources\" title=\"Source: vault note drivendata-dat-parkinsons-challenge\">[src]</a></sup>.</li>\n<li><strong>Let the stack do the calibration.</strong> The stack's CNN weight sits below 1, which works like temperature scaling. So there is no separate calibration step to fit and maintain.</li>\n<li><strong>Choose calibrators out of sample.</strong> Early on, isotonic regression was picked because it had been scored on its own training predictions. Under cross-validation it did worse than no calibration: 0.3520 against 0.3271 log loss<sup class=\"cite\"><a href=\"#sources\" title=\"Source: vault note drivendata-dat-parkinsons-challenge\">[src]</a></sup>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Result</h2>\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-title\">Baseline model: strong ranking on most acquisition families, weakest on the small 128 @ 1.5 mm family</div><div class=\"dotplot\"><div class=\"dp-legend\"><i></i>All scans, baseline 0.9302</div><div class=\"dp-row dp-row--axis\"><div class=\"dp-label dp-axis-title\">AUROC (higher is better)</div><div class=\"dp-track dp-axis\"><span class=\"dp-tick\" style=\"left:0.00%\">0.80</span><span class=\"dp-tick\" style=\"left:25.00%\">0.85</span><span class=\"dp-tick\" style=\"left:50.00%\">0.90</span><span class=\"dp-tick\" style=\"left:75.00%\">0.95</span><span class=\"dp-tick\" style=\"left:100.00%\">1.00</span></div><div></div></div><div class=\"dp-row\"><div class=\"dp-label\"><span>256 @ 2.5 mm</span><span class=\"dp-sub\">n = 460 · ECE 0.0509</span></div><div class=\"dp-track\"><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:0.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:25.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:50.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:75.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:100.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-ref\" style=\"left:65.10%\"></span><span class=\"dp-dot\" style=\"left:58.80%\" title=\"256 @ 2.5 mm: 0.9176\"></span></div><div class=\"dp-value\">0.9176</div></div><div class=\"dp-row\"><div class=\"dp-label\"><span>128 @ 3.9 mm</span><span class=\"dp-sub\">n = 325 · ECE 0.0544</span></div><div class=\"dp-track\"><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:0.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:25.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:50.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:75.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:100.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-ref\" style=\"left:65.10%\"></span><span class=\"dp-dot\" style=\"left:63.85%\" title=\"128 @ 3.9 mm: 0.9277\"></span></div><div class=\"dp-value\">0.9277</div></div><div class=\"dp-row\"><div class=\"dp-label\"><span>128 @ 2.3 mm</span><span class=\"dp-sub\">n = 207 · ECE 0.0397</span></div><div class=\"dp-track\"><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:0.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:25.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:50.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:75.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:100.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-ref\" style=\"left:65.10%\"></span><span class=\"dp-dot\" style=\"left:69.80%\" title=\"128 @ 2.3 mm: 0.9396\"></span></div><div class=\"dp-value\">0.9396</div></div><div class=\"dp-row\"><div class=\"dp-label\"><span>128 @ 2.4 mm</span><span class=\"dp-sub\">n = 149 · ECE 0.0407</span></div><div class=\"dp-track\"><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:0.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:25.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:50.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:75.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:100.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-ref\" style=\"left:65.10%\"></span><span class=\"dp-dot\" style=\"left:78.00%\" title=\"128 @ 2.4 mm: 0.9560\"></span></div><div class=\"dp-value\">0.9560</div></div><div class=\"dp-row\"><div class=\"dp-label\"><span>Small families, pooled</span><span class=\"dp-sub\">n = 125 · ECE 0.0676</span></div><div class=\"dp-track\"><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:0.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:25.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:50.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:75.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:100.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-ref\" style=\"left:65.10%\"></span><span class=\"dp-dot\" style=\"left:54.85%\" title=\"Small families, pooled: 0.9097\"></span></div><div class=\"dp-value\">0.9097</div></div><div class=\"dp-row\"><div class=\"dp-label\"><span>var @ 2.5 mm</span><span class=\"dp-sub\">n = 66 · ECE 0.0930</span></div><div class=\"dp-track\"><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:0.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:25.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:50.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:75.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:100.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-ref\" style=\"left:65.10%\"></span><span class=\"dp-dot\" style=\"left:73.15%\" title=\"var @ 2.5 mm: 0.9463\"></span></div><div class=\"dp-value\">0.9463</div></div><div class=\"dp-row dp-row--hot\"><div class=\"dp-label\"><span>128 @ 1.5 mm</span><span class=\"dp-sub\">n = 30 · ECE 0.1552</span></div><div class=\"dp-track\"><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:0.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:25.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:50.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:75.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:100.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-ref\" style=\"left:65.10%\"></span><span class=\"dp-dot\" style=\"left:18.65%\" title=\"128 @ 1.5 mm: 0.8373\"></span></div><div class=\"dp-value\">0.8373</div></div></div><figcaption>Run 1 baseline, stratified OOF, so every family was seen in training. Families are named as recorded: 21 in total, the 6 with n ≥ 30 shown and the rest pooled. Per-family results for the final model are not recorded.</figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>The final model ranks scans well: out-of-fold AUROC 0.9455<sup class=\"cite\"><a href=\"#sources\" title=\"Source: vault note drivendata-dat-parkinsons-challenge\">[src]</a></sup>. AUROC is the chance that a random abnormal scan scores above a random normal one; 1 is perfect. The CNN ensemble's probabilities are close to honest. ECE, the average gap between predicted probability and the rate actually observed, is 0.0187 for the CNN ensemble. For the baseline, calibrating each family with a temperature fitted only on the other families cost just +0.0006 log loss overall, so the calibration carries over to acquisitions it was not fitted on<sup class=\"cite\"><a href=\"#sources\" title=\"Source: vault note drivendata-dat-parkinsons-challenge\">[src]</a></sup>.</p>\n<p>The weak spots are the small families. The 30-scan 1.5 mm family and the pooled small families have the lowest AUROC and the highest ECE, so a probability on an uncommon acquisition deserves less trust. The per-family breakdown exists only for the baseline, and every family was seen in training<sup class=\"cite\"><a href=\"#sources\" title=\"Source: vault note drivendata-dat-parkinsons-challenge\">[src]</a></sup>. On the leaderboard my entry finished #159 of 1009 (top 16%), with private scores worse than public by a similar margin for every build<sup class=\"cite\"><a href=\"#sources\" title=\"Source: vault note drivendata-dat-parkinsons-challenge\">[src]</a></sup>.</p>\n<h2>What I learned</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Diversity beats quality in a stack.</strong> The trees and the second CNN run were each weaker alone, yet they gave the largest gains, because their errors fell in different places.</li>\n<li><strong>Pooled calibration hides the groups that matter.</strong> The baseline looked well calibrated on all scans together, yet its ECE on the 30-scan 1.5 mm family was 0.1552<sup class=\"cite\"><a href=\"#sources\" title=\"Source: vault note drivendata-dat-parkinsons-challenge\">[src]</a></sup>. I only broke results down by family for the baseline, so I cannot say whether the final model closes that gap.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Tools</h2>\n<p>Python, PyTorch, LightGBM, scikit-learn, NumPy, pandas, SciPy, pytest, Docker, Claude Code. The assistant never saw competition data. It wrote scripts and received only aggregate summaries.</p>\n<h2>Links</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Competition: <a href=\"https://www.drivendata.org/competitions/311/dat-parkinsons-challenge/\">https://www.drivendata.org/competitions/311/dat-parkinsons-challenge/</a></li>\n<li>Code repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/feitandodatascience/dat-parkinsons-challenge\">https://github.com/feitandodatascience/dat-parkinsons-challenge</a></li>\n</ul>",
  "sources": [
    "drivendata-dat-parkinsons-challenge"
  ]
}
